DrawTest
├── When called before the daily deadline
│   └── It should revert.
├── When anyone calls at the deadline
│   └── It should lock the highest bid and request two random words.
├── When a request is already pending
│   └── It should revert.
├── When the subscription request fails
│   └── It should preserve the winner funds and deadline.
├── When the day has no bids
│   └── It should advance the day without requesting randomness.
├── When the day has no inventory
│   └── It should advance the day without requesting randomness.
├── When an unauthorized account fulfills
│   └── It should revert.
├── When the wrong request is fulfilled
│   └── It should leave the draw waiting.
├── When zero randomness is returned
│   └── It should select a valid token including token zero.
├── When randomness is duplicated
│   └── It should preserve the first result.
├── When finalization precedes randomness
│   └── It should revert.
├── When anyone finalizes a ready draw
│   └── It should reserve one token and recognize only the winning payment.
├── When a draw is finalized twice
│   └── It should revert.
├── When multiple days are drawn
│   └── It should never assign the same token twice.
├── When a late caller starts a draw
│   └── It should schedule the next draw a full day later.
└── When a pending draw outlasts the next cutoff
    └── It should freeze changes to next day bids.
